{
  "dom_id": "question-213547",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "Consider a relation $R$ that is defined on the set $A=\\{6,7,8\\}.$ Given that $R$ is antisymmetric, enter the missing values in the adjacency matrix. \n\n**Note**: If there is not enough information to determine a particular cell's value, then select the question mark $(\\text{?}).$\n\n|  | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $6$ | $1$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $7$ | {{field-2}} | $1$ | $0$ |\n| $8$ | $1$ | {{field-3}} | $1$ |",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
